{"strongs": "H0270", "word": "אָחַז", "translit": "a.chaz", "root": "אחה", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "grasp, take hold, take posses-sion", "definition": "אָחַז 68 verb grasp, take hold, take posses-sion (Arabic , Sabean אחֿדֿ SabDenkm 39 , Aramaic אֲחַד , Assyrian a—azu , Ethiopic ) — Qal Perfect אָחַז Exod 15:14 +; אָֽחֲזָה Job 23:11 ; Isa 33:14 suffix אֲחָזַנִי 2Sam 1:9 1 singular suffix אֲחַזְתִּיו Song 3:4 ,etc.; Imperfect יאֹחֵז Job 17:9 +; וַיּ֫אֹחֶז 2Sam 6:6 3 feminine singular תּאֹחֵז Deut 32:41 וַתּאֹחֶז Ruth 3:15 וַתֹּחֶז 2Sam 20:9 וָאֹחֵז Judg 20:6 יאֹחֵזוּן Isa 13:8 suffix יאֹחֲזֵ֫מוֺ Exod 15:15 יאֹחֱזוּךְ Jer 13:21 , etc.; — as ׳ פ guttural וַיֶּאֱחֹז Judg 16:3 ; 1Kgs 6:10 2 masculine singular תֶּאֱחֹז Eccl 7:18 Infinitive אֲחֹז 1Kgs 6:6 אֱחֹז 1Chr 13:9 + 3 t.; Imperative אֱחֹז Exod 4:4 ; 2Sam 2:21 , אֶחֳזִיֿ Ruth 3:15 אֶחֱזוּ Song 2:15 אֱחֹ֑זוּ Neh 7:3 Participle active אֹחֵז 2Chr 25:5 passive אָחוּז Esth 1:6 , etc.; — grasp, take hold of , followed by בְּ Gen 25:26 ; Exod 4:4 (both J ) Judg 16:3 ; Judg 20:6 ( = וַיַּחֲזֵק בְּ Judg 19:29 ) 2Sam 4:10 ; 2Sam 6:6 ; 2Sam 20:9 ; 1Kgs 1:51 ; Ruth 3:15 (twice in verse); 1Kgs 6:6 of beams having hold in a wall; (compare בֵּית אֲבָנִים יֶָֽחֱזֶה֑ Job 8:17 Hoffm reads יֹחֲזָה = ׳ יאֹ ); also Song 7:9 of taking hold of branches, in metaphor; poetic, figurative, of God's seizing man in wrath Job 16:12 taking hold graciously Ps 73:23 taking hold of judgment Deut 32:41 subject man בַּאֲשֻׁרוֺ אָֽחֲזָה רַגְלִי Job 23:11 (|| דַּרְכּוֺ שָׁמַרְתִּי compare also Job 17:9 ); of taking hold of folly Eccl 2:3 compare Eccl 7:18 subject הַשַּׁחַר Job 38:13 , לֶאֱחֹו בְּכַנְפוֺת הָאָ֑רֶץ ; also followed by accusative Judg 1:6 ; Judg 12:6 ; Judg 16:21 ; 2Sam 2:21 ; Isa 5:29 ; Song 2:15 ; Song 3:4 ; 1Chr 13:9 ; 2Chr 25:5 ; Ps 56:1 ; Ps 137:9 compare 1Kgs 6:10 (compare v 1Kgs 6:6 above), subject הַיָּצוּעַ , אֶתֿ ׳ וַיֶּא הַבַּיִת בַּעֲצֵי אֲרָזִים ; of a snare catching the heel, in metaphor Job 18:9 figurative, subject God Ps 77:5 God's hand Ps 139:10 subject pain, sorrow, fear, etc. Exod 15:14 ; Exod 15:15 ; 2Sam 1:9 ; Job 21:6 ; Job 30:16 ; Ps 48:7 ; Ps 119:53 ; Isa 21:3 ; Isa 33:14 ; Jer 13:21 ; Jer 49:24 subject man, object fear, etc. Job 18:20 ; Isa 13:8 object דֶּרֶךְ take one's way Job 17:9 יאֹחֵז צַדִּיק דַּרְכּוֺ AV RV hold on his way (compare Job 23:11 above, & Assyrian ƒabâtu ur—u , e. g. V. R:1, 74); — absolute Neh 7:3 of barring gates; passive participle caught Eccl 9:12 fastened, held Esth 1:6 taken (by lot) 1Chr 24:6 (3 t. in verse) (on text see Öttli ); taken out of a number Num 31:30 ; Num 31:47 participle active of same form אֲחֻזֵי חֶרֶב Song 3:8 compare Thes Ba NB 175 & Ethiopic Participle .; similarly Aramaic אָחִיד , e.g. ᵑ7 Amos 2:5 e.g. ᵑ6 Judg 8:10 ; 1Chr 5:18 & Ezek 41:6 (twice in verse) (but see Co ). Niph`al Perfect 3 plural נאֹחֲזוּ Josh 22:9 ׳ וְנאֹ (consecutive) Num 32:30 Imperfect וַיֵּאָחֲזוּ Gen 47:27 Imperative הֵאָֽחֲזוּ Gen 34:10 ; Josh 22:19 Participle נֶאֱחָז Gen 22:13 נֶאֱחָזִים Eccl 9:12 — be caught Gen 22:13 ; Eccl 9:12 elsewhere have possessions Gen 34:10 ; Gen 47:27 ; Num 32:30 ; Josh 22:9 ; Josh 22:19 ( P ). Pi`el Participle מְאַחֵז Job 26:9 with accusative enclose, overlay (so Assyrian Dl W, p. 294 , compare Arabic , shut ). Hoph`al Participle plural מָאֳחָזִים 2Chr 9:18 fastened to followed by לְ .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB317')\">BDB317</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H270')\">H270</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB316')\">BDB316</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB318')\">BDB318</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>אָחַז</bdbheb><sub>68</sub> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>grasp, take hold, take posses-sion</highlightword> (Arabic <placeholder145/>, Sabean <bdbheb>אחֿדֿ</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('SabDenkm')\">SabDenkm<sup>39</sup></lookup>, Aramaic <bdbarc>אֲחַד</bdbarc>, <placeholder146/> Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>a—azu</highlight></transliteration